The [[Pestilence Flask]] is an epic [[Potion]] available in the shop for all classes. It inflicts {{icon/poison}} on the opponent, and a smaller amount to the player, when the opponent heals. The amount isn't all that significant, so it's best to either abuse it with potion synergies (like [[Heavy Drinking]]) in a {{icon/poison}} build, or use it as a crafting material.

The [[Pestilence Flask]] can combine with the [[Dagger]], [[Spear]], [[Magic Staff]], [[Shortbow]], or [[Bow and Arrow]] to create generally improved {{icon/poison}}-inflicting weapons.

[[Reaper]]s can combine the [[Fly Agaric]] with the [[Pestilence Flask]] or catalytically convert the [[Pestilence Flask]] using the [[Cauldron]] into the [[Strong Pestilence Flask]], which is the same except it inflicts twice the {{icon/poison}} to the opponent.

[[Engineer]]s can combine the [[Pestilence Flask]] with a [[Stone]] and a [[Resistor]] to craft the [[Poison Grenade]], which is a good way of giving a large bulk of {{icon/poison}} to the opponent, though it will also poison the user themselves.

Like all [[Potion]]s, when used, it will apply the affect of the [[Potion]] above it, without consuming the one above. This adjacency is unlike most in that the {{icon/star}} will always be placed above the [[Potion]], rather than rotating along with the item. The [[Pestilence Flask]] has a relatively easy trigger condition, making it good for triggering other [[Potion]]s early in the fight.
